          "name" : "forceMove",
          "expression" : "= forceMove",
          "description" : "This means that an address can be modified or explicitly moved.\n\n- In case of modifications, current address data is overwritten with the new address data.\n- In case of relocation, the validity of the previous address data is ended and a new data record is created with the new address data valid from indicated date.\n\n- It is dependent on bank parameterisation how old previous address data can be and still be modifiable.\n- If this period of time has already been exceeded, i.e. the address data is older than permitted in the parameterisation, then a relocation is automatically carried out even if no relocation is explicitly desired via parameter forceMove.\n- If an address data modification is permitted on the basis of the parameterisation, relocation can be forced using this parameter so that the previous address data remains in an expired data record.",
