      "topicName" : "swisscom-fil-is-clientV1.PutClientsClientKey",
      "ownerDescr" : "Opening of a new client master record **with** prior reservation of the client identification or modification of an existing client master record.\nThe required input structure is determined accordingly with the value of the attribute *useCase*, you can also provide the *clientType* and optional *isUpdate* flag instead.\n\nWhen opening a new client master record, it is ensured with a UUID in the request header 'Request-Id' that the request is executed a maximum of one time.\n\nWhen modifying an existing client master record, it is ensured with the current resource version in the request 'If-Match' that no 'lost update' situation can arise.\nThe resource version needs to be read in advance using the corresponding GET request, which returns it as *etag* in the response header.\n\nThe request must contain exactly one of the two request headers 'Request-Id' or 'If-Match'.\n\nSample request: PUT /banks/949/clients/123456789",
      "routing" : [
        "useCase",
        "clientType"
      ]
    },
