        },
        {
          "name" : "removalFilterPortfolio",
          "type" : "Option[RemovalStatusUnion]",
          "description" : "List of portfolio removal status to filter by;\nEnables filtering on the basis of the portfolio removal statuses.\nWithout a given value, no filtering is applied.\n\nBear in mind that only the following combinations are legal:\n  - ACTIVE|PROV_CLOSED|DEF_CLOSED\n  - DEF_CLOSED\n  - ACTIVE|PROV_CLOSED",
          "example" : "None"
        },
        {
          "name" : "removalFilterAccount",
          "type" : "Option[RemovalStatusUnion]",
          "description" : "List of account removal status to filter by;\nEnables filtering on the basis of the account removal statuses.\nWithout a given value, no filtering is applied.\n\nThe former enum values \"DEF_CLOSED_OR_PROV_CLOSED\",\n\"ACTIVE_OR_PROV_CLOSED\" and\n\"ACTIVE_OR_PROV_CLOSED_OR_RECENTLY_DEF_CLOSED\" are still working as before but deprecated.\n\nBear in mind that the combination \"ACTIVE|DEF_CLOSED\" is illegal.\n\nIf you don't specify `removalFilterAccount` or `removalFilterPortfolio`, it sets `removalFilterAccount` to `ACTIVE`.",
          "example" : "None"
        }
      ],
      "topicName" : "valiant-fil-is-accountAndPortfolioV3.GetAccounts",
      "ownerDescr" : "Read overview of a client's accounts. \nYou can filter by removal status (portfolio and/or account) as well as by portfolio.\n\nSample request: GET /banks/949/accounts/123456789/accounts?removalFilterAccount=PROV_CLOSED\n\nBreaking Changes to V2:\n - `removalFilterPortfolio` /  `removalFilterAccount`:\n   now you must send a Seq of RemovalStatus instead of a single RemovalStatus - and also the status have changed."
    },
